{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd938575adaa6106","type":"tool_result","content":"16:**Detailed**: Feast consists of two primary runtime components: a Go-based Kubernetes operator (`feast-operator`) and a multi-language feature serving stack. The operator manages `FeatureStore` custom resources (API group `feast.dev`, versions `v1` and `v1alpha1`) and reconciles them into Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, RBAC resources, HorizontalPodAutoscalers, PodDisruptionBudgets, CronJobs, and OpenShift Routes. The `FeatureStoreReconciler` watches the FeatureStore CR and owns 12 dependent Kubernetes resource types; a secondary `NotebookConfigMapReconciler` watches FeatureStore CRs and ConfigMaps to inject Feast client configuration into Kubeflow Notebook workbenches. The serving stack exposes both HTTP and gRPC interfaces: a Go feature server handles online feature retrieval (`/get-online-features`, `/health`) with Prometheus metrics, while a Python FastAPI/Starlette server exposes a comprehensive REST API for registry management, feature serving, monitoring, lineage tracking, and a UI. The Python SDK also provides gRPC services for registry, serving, transformation, and health checking. Authentication is CRD-configurable: operators select exactly one of Kubernetes RBAC or OIDC authorization, enforced by the Python permissions framework (`SecurityManager`, `AuthManager`), with TLS optionally configured via Secret references or OpenShift service serving certificates. [source: infra/feast-operator/api/v1alpha1/featurestore_types.go:611-634, 636-657, 706, infra/feast-operator/internal/controller/featurestore_controller.go:366-376, sdk/python/feast/permissions/server/utils.py:45-52]\n24:The authentication model is noteworthy for its configurability and its security implications. The `AuthzConfig` CRD field enforces exactly one of Kubernetes RBAC or OIDC authorization via a kubebuilder validation rule. The Python permissions framework (`SecurityManager` → `AuthManager`) supports three runtime modes: `no_auth` (AllowAll), `oidc` (OIDC token parsing via PyJWT), and `kubernetes` (Kubernetes token validation). However, the Go feature server's gRPC and HTTP handler chains have no authentication interceptors or middleware — they rely on network-level isolation or external enforcement. The operator's own metrics endpoint is secured via controller-runtime's TokenReview/SubjectAccessReview filter with self-signed TLS. Health and readiness probes are intentionally unauthenticated.\n26:The operator manages RBAC extensively: the `feast-operator-manager-role` ClusterRole grants 23 rules spanning core resources, CRDs (feast.dev, kubeflow.org, monitoring.coreos.com, sparkoperator.k8s.io), OpenShift APIs (routes, apiservers), and RBAC management (ClusterRoles, ClusterRoleBindings, Roles, RoleBindings). This broad RBAC surface enables the operator to create per-namespace authorization structures when Kubernetes RBAC auth is selected. External integrations include online stores (PostgreSQL, Redis/Valkey), object storage registries (S3, GCS), compute engines (Ray, Kubernetes Jobs, Spark), and monitoring (prometheus-operator ServiceMonitors). [source: infra/feast-operator/internal/controller/featurestore_controller.go:366-376, infra/feast-operator/api/v1alpha1/featurestore_types.go:611-634, sdk/python/feast/permissions/server/utils.py:45-63, sdk/python/feast/permissions/auth/auth_manager.py:60-68, go/internal/feast/server/http_server.go:388-389, infra/feast-operator/config/rbac/role.yaml:2]\n498:### RBAC - Cluster Roles\n522:| feast-operator-manager-role | rbac.authorization.k8s.io | clusterrolebindings, clusterroles, rolebindings, roles, subjectaccessreviews | create, delete, get, list, update, watch |\n527:| feast-operator-featurestore-editor-role | feast.dev | featurestores | create, delete, get, list, patch, update, watch |\n528:| feast-operator-featurestore-editor-role | feast.dev | featurestores/status | get |\n529:| feast-operator-featurestore-viewer-role | feast.dev | featurestores | get, list, watch |\n530:| feast-operator-featurestore-viewer-role | feast.dev | featurestores/status | get |\n531:| featurestore-editor-role | feast.dev | featurestores | create, delete, get, list, patch, update, watch |\n532:| featurestore-editor-role | feast.dev | featurestores/status | get |\n533:| featurestore-viewer-role | feast.dev | featurestores | get, list, watch |\n534:| featurestore-viewer-role | feast.dev | featurestores/status | get |\n557:| manager-role | rbac.authorization.k8s.io | clusterrolebindings, clusterroles, rolebindings, roles, subjectaccessreviews | create, delete, get, list, update, watch |\n567:### RBAC - Role Bindings\n600:| Feast services (CRD-configured) | ALL | Configurable: Kubernetes RBAC or OIDC | CRD-selected service authorization | Exactly one of Kubernetes RBAC roles or an OIDC Secret reference is required |\n603:| Kubernetes API | REST | ServiceAccount token (in-cluster) | kube-apiserver | RBAC enforced via feast-operator-manager-role ClusterRole; SA feast-operator-controller-manager |\n604:| :8443/metrics | GET | TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview (controller-runtime authn/authz filter) | controller-runtime metrics authn/authz filter | RBAC via feast-operator-metrics-auth-role; exposed by Service feast-operator-controller-manager-metrics-service; controller-runtime generated self-signed TLS certificate |\n612:| rbac-ref | kubernetes | Kubernetes client library (RBAC capable) | dependency-signal |\n680:| 1 | Client | Python feature server | 6566 | HTTP/HTTPS | Configurable TLS | Configurable (OIDC/Kubernetes RBAC/None) |\n733:| rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1/ClusterRole | Resource CRUD |  |  |  | Unknown | create, delete, get, update operations by FeastAuthorization |\n734:| rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1/ClusterRoleBinding | Resource CRUD |  |  |  | Unknown | create, delete, get, update operations by FeastAuthorization |\n735:| rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1/Role | Controller watch (Owns) |  |  | Kubernetes API | TLS | FeatureStoreReconciler |\n736:| rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1/Role | Resource CRUD |  |  |  | Unknown | create, delete, get, list, update operations by FeastAuthorization, FeastServices |\n737:| rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1/RoleBinding | Controller watch (Owns) |  |  | Kubernetes API | TLS | FeatureStoreReconciler |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83035eeaf0612315","agent_id":"af9a83e3527bcd761","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"5e6a9fe5-7058-4ece-9ee3-1739ea9db298","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:26:17.468Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd938575adaa6106","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007 into epics"}
