{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-720fda0f-e229-4963-b086-cace594b41fe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e695c98b3b77e4f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-5ww_zm6p/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E001.md","content":"# Resolve FeatureStore CRD form scope and operator validation questions\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the open questions that determine what the Feature Store admin create form exposes and confirm that the existing Feast operator safely handles dashboard-created instances. It produces a single findings-and-recommendations deliverable owned by Feature Store Engineering (with PM input on the field-subset decision) that the dashboard create-wizard implementation builds against. The strategy explicitly flags these as open questions and \"needs validation\" assumptions; their answers change the scope of the guided form wizard, so this is a true gate.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Recommend whether the TP create form should expose the full `FeatureStore` CRD (feast.dev/v1) spec or a curated subset, with the recommended field list and sensible defaults covering: namespace, registry type, online store backend (Redis, PostgreSQL, DynamoDB, SQLite), offline store backend, authorization mode (OIDC vs Kubernetes RBAC), TLS settings, scaling configuration (replicas, HPA), and materialization CronJob scheduling.\n- Document CRD schema constraints the form must enforce (required fields, valid backend combinations, scaling prerequisites), derived from the feast.dev/v1 OpenAPI schema.\n- Identify backend combinations that should be restricted or flagged in the form (e.g., SQLite as development-only, not production-suitable).\n- Confirm the stability of the FeatureStore v1 API for the RHOAI 3.5 cycle (v1alpha1 is deprecated; v1 shipped in 3.5-ea.1 with Feast 0.63.0) and record a version-pin recommendation.\n- Validate that the feast-operator correctly reconciles `FeatureStore` CRs created through the Kubernetes API by the dashboard (not just kubectl/GitOps), and that CRD webhook validation is sufficient for UI-submitted resources — recording a pass/fail result and any gaps.\n- Document CRD field mutability (which fields are immutable after creation) to inform the explicitly deferred follow-on edit capability — informational only, edit is out of TP scope.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A findings document enumerates the recommended form field set with per-field CRD constraints, traceable to the feast.dev/v1 OpenAPI schema.\n- Backend combination restrictions (or guidance flags) are documented with rationale.\n- Operator reconciliation of dashboard-created FeatureStore CRs is exercised on a test cluster and the pass/fail result, including any webhook-validation gaps and their client-side mitigation, is recorded.\n- A CRD stability assessment for the RHOAI 3.5 cycle is recorded with a version-pin recommendation.\n- The curated-subset vs full-field-set decision is recorded with PM sign-off.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- De-risks and shapes HLR-1 (P0: guided create form wizard) — the field-set recommendation defines the wizard's scope.\n- Supports HLR-5 (P0: readiness status from `.status.conditions`) — confirms the status surface the management pages render.\n- Supports HLR-8 (P2: inline validation for CRD schema constraints) — supplies the constraint set the form validates against.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47080,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83035eeaf0612315","agent_id":"af9a83e3527bcd761","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"1ef8cd5c-935a-46c8-9d77-5e1d3342218e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:28:15.351Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007 into epics"}
