{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-4ca46d1b-e41b-40e0-804c-3cf66fc701d2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaef1c5b5d894dc0","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-5ww_zm6p/artifacts/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-5ww_zm6p/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E002.md","content":"# Assess prototype PR #7013 alignment with the formal implementation approach\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation determines how much of the validated engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) can be reused for the formal Feature Store admin UI implementation, and whether the prototype's approach matches the strategy's formal path (K8s API pass-through for CRUD, `/api/featurestores` read proxy, `secureAdminRoute` gating, feature-flag rollout). The strategy lists prototype alignment as an assumption needing validation with the Dashboard and Feature Store engineering leads; the answer changes the implementation approach of the frontend epics, so this is a true gate.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Review the prototype PR #7013 code against the strategy's formal approach: CRUD via the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through, reads via the existing `/api/featurestores` proxy, admin/viewer gating via `secureAdminRoute` and the admin status check, and feature-flag gating in `OdhDashboardConfig`.\n- Produce a reuse inventory: which prototype components, hooks, pages, and patterns can be carried into the formal implementation as-is, which need rework, and which diverge from the formal path and must be rebuilt.\n- Identify any architectural divergences (e.g., new backend routes, bypassed RBAC patterns, hardcoded config) and their remediation cost.\n- Record an engineering-lead confirmation (Dashboard + Feature Store) that the prototype may serve as the reference implementation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A findings document maps each prototype surface (create flow, list, detail, delete, status handling) to a disposition: reuse as-is / rework / rebuild, with rationale.\n- Any divergence between the prototype and the formal approach (API routing, authorization, feature gating) is enumerated with the corrective action required.\n- Engineering-lead sign-off on using the prototype as the implementation reference is recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- De-risks HLR-1 through HLR-5 (P0: create wizard, list page, detail view, delete flow, status tracking) — the alignment finding determines the implementation approach for all admin UI frontend surfaces.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47922,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83035eeaf0612315","agent_id":"af9a83e3527bcd761","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"05019e90-a739-44f7-b4de-99b400cd5f20","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:28:24.851Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007 into epics"}
