{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f5269db7-aaec-418e-9258-32ce3ce0b330","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-97f99816a2163819","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-5ww_zm6p/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E004.md","content":"# Extend odh-dashboard RBAC and feature-flag manifests for Feature Store admin CRUD\n\n## Description\n\nExtends the odh-dashboard Kubernetes manifests so platform administrators can perform CRUD operations on `FeatureStore` custom resources through the dashboard, and gates the new admin UI behind an `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag for progressive rollout. This is a manifest-only change: no new backend routes are needed — CRUD flows through the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through proxy with the user's forwarded token, and reads continue to use the existing `/api/featurestores` proxy.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Update `manifests/core-bases/base/sa-rbac/cluster-role.yaml` to add `create, update, patch, delete` verbs for `feast.dev/featurestores` to the dashboard's ClusterRole (it currently grants only `get, list, watch`). Use the feast-operator's `featurestore-editor-role` ClusterRole as the reference for the minimum required permission set.\n- Preserve the viewer tier: non-admin users remain limited to the existing `featurestore-viewer-role` (`get, list, watch` on `featurestores` and `featurestores/status`) — no viewer permission expansion.\n- Add the Feature Store admin UI feature flag default in `OdhDashboardConfig` so clusters without the Feast component enabled see no UI changes (backwards compatibility / progressive rollout).\n- No changes to the Feast CRD schema or operator behavior; no new BFF sidecar or Go module (FIPS posture unchanged).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The dashboard ClusterRole grants `create, update, patch, delete` (plus existing read verbs) on `feast.dev/featurestores`, matching or exceeding the `featurestore-editor-role` reference permission set.\n- A user bound only to the viewer role remains unable to create, update, or delete `FeatureStore` CRs via the Kubernetes API (enforcement is at the K8s API level via the forwarded token, not UI hiding).\n- The admin UI is gated behind the `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag and is not visible when the flag is disabled or the Feast component is absent.\n- Manifests render and apply cleanly; no new backend routes, containers, or external network connections are introduced.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables HLR-1 (P0: deploy FeatureStore via dashboard) — write verbs required for create.\n- Enables HLR-4 (P0: delete FeatureStore from dashboard) — delete verb required.\n- Supports HLR-6 (P1: viewers browse but cannot create/delete) — viewer tier stays read-only at the RBAC level.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49234,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83035eeaf0612315","agent_id":"af9a83e3527bcd761","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"8aac94f0-4449-4726-a744-ea5d5f18ac46","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:28:45.748Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007 into epics"}
