dashboard's static assets — no external network fetches (air-gapped support).\n- Gate the wizard behind the `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag.\n- Reuse prototype components where the alignment assessment confirms architectural fit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A platform admin can complete the wizard and submit a valid `FeatureStore` CR to the Kubernetes API from the dashboard — no YAML editing or CLI access required; the form renders all required CRD fields per the investigation's field-set recommendation without error.\n- Invalid input is blocked before submission with inline guidance derived from the CRD schema; if the Kubernetes API rejects a submitted CR, the validation error is surfaced in the UI.\n- The wizard functions on a disconnected/air-gapped cluster — no form options, validation rules, or UI assets require external network access.\n- A non-admin (viewer) user does not see the create action.\n- The wizard is hidden when the feature flag is disabled.\n- End-to-end create is verified against a cluster with the extended dashboard ClusterRole applied (write verbs on `feast.dev/featurestores`).\n- Implementation follows the formal approach (K8s API pass-through, no new backend routes, no new BFF sidecar).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): deploy a new FeatureStore instance via guided form wizard.\n- HLR-6 (P1, viewer portion): create action hidden for non-admin users.\n- HLR-7 (P1, form portion): functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments.\n- HLR-8 (P2): inline guidance for CRD schema constraints — bundled here because it is the same form surface as HLR-1.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49959,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83035eeaf0612315","agent_id":"af9a83e3527bcd761","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"a00944cb-4608-4631-b0b4-f6f18fb0fcf3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:28:57.714Z","subagent_type":"ge