{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d408ea8d-437a-424e-b303-204b7a39b94b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5aeec692e8b8791","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8007-5ww_zm6p/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8007-E006.md","content":"# Feature Store management pages: list, detail/inspect, delete, status tracking\n\n## Description\n\nImplements the Feature Store management surface in the RHOAI dashboard: a list page showing all `FeatureStore` instances across namespaces accessible to the user, a read-only detail/inspect view of any instance's full spec and status, an admin-initiated delete flow with confirmation dialog, and real-time deployment-progress tracking from `.status.conditions`. Reads use the existing dashboard K8s watch/list patterns; delete sends a `DELETE` to the Kubernetes API through the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through, with the feast-operator handling resource cleanup via finalizers. Builds against the UXD designs and reuses the validated engineering prototype wherever the alignment assessment confirms it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build the management list page per the UXD designs: rows showing name, namespace, deployment status, and creation timestamp, with inspect and delete row actions; scoped to namespaces the user can access.\n- Implement status polling via the dashboard's existing K8s watch/list patterns so readiness state (`.status.conditions`) updates in real time without manual refresh, including the \"Deploying\" → \"Ready\" progression after creation.\n- Build the read-only detail/inspect view: full `FeatureStore` CR spec (online/offline store backends, registry type, authorization mode, scaling, TLS status, materialization schedule) and current status conditions, rendered without truncation; link to the Feast UI Route for browsing feature metadata when available.\n- Implement the delete flow with a confirmation dialog; deletion relies on the feast-operator's finalizer-based cleanup of owned resources (Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, CronJobs, HPAs, PDBs, RBAC, Routes).\n- Gate write controls (delete action) on platform-admin status; non-admin (viewer) users see list and detail views without write controls.\n- Gate the pages behind the `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag; bundle all assets (air-gapped support); no external network fetches.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The management page lists all FeatureStore instances in namespaces the admin can access, matching `kubectl get featurestores -A` output for those namespaces, with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp.\n- After a new instance is created, the list shows it with a deploying status that transitions to ready as `.status.conditions` update, within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle and without manual refresh.\n- The detail view renders all spec fields and status conditions of the `FeatureStore` CR in read-only form without truncation.\n- Delete with confirmation removes the `FeatureStore` CR via the Kubernetes API; the instance disappears from the list and `kubectl get featurestore <name> -n <ns>` returns NotFound, with operator-owned resources cleaned up.\n- A non-admin (viewer) user can browse the list and detail views but sees no delete action.\n- The pages function on a disconnected/air-gapped cluster — no UI assets or data fetches require external network access.\n- The pages are hidden when the feature flag is disabled.\n- End-to-end delete is verified against a cluster with the extended dashboard ClusterRole applied.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): view all FeatureStore instances in a management page.\n- HLR-3 (P0): inspect configuration in a read-only detail view.\n- HLR-4 (P0): delete a FeatureStore instance with confirmation dialog.\n- HLR-5 (P0): deployment progress / readiness visible in real time.\n- HLR-6 (P1, browse portion): viewers can browse list and detail without delete actions.\n- HLR-7 (P1, page portion): functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50810,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83035eeaf0612315","agent_id":"af9a83e3527bcd761","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"d0d948e7-a3ec-481d-94d5-4aa2219c0437","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:29:11.035Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007 into epics"}
