st suites covering CRUD flows, viewer/admin RBAC enforcement, and status accuracy pass, with results recorded.\n- A FeatureStore instance is successfully deployed from the dashboard on an air-gapped cluster with no external connectivity — the disconnected-environment acceptance criterion from the strategy is demonstrated end to end.\n- Direct Kubernetes API write attempts by a viewer-role user are rejected (RBAC enforced at the API level, not only UI hiding).\n- Feature-flag gating behaves as specified (no UI changes on clusters without the Feast component enabled).\n- Dashboard pod resource consumption in QE environments is recorded and shows no unexpected growth attributable to the admin UI.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Validates HLR-1 through HLR-5 (P0: create, list, inspect, delete, status tracking) — functional verification of each flow.\n- Validates HLR-6 (P1: viewer browse-only enforcement, including API-level bypass attempts).\n- Validates HLR-7 (P1: disconnected/air-gapped operation) — the dedicated air-gapped test pass.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51764,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83035eeaf0612315","agent_id":"af9a83e3527bcd761","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"63cd35e4-461b-4f1f-a1f0-23f6877b10b6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:29:21.400Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8007 into epics"}
