{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bafb6cdf8ea51c36","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E004\n3\ttitle: Extend odh-dashboard RBAC and feature-flag manifests for Feature Store admin\n4\t  CRUD\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n7\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Extend odh-dashboard RBAC and feature-flag manifests for Feature Store admin CRUD\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tExtends the odh-dashboard Kubernetes manifests so platform administrators can perform CRUD operations on `FeatureStore` custom resources through the dashboard, and gates the new admin UI behind an `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag for progressive rollout. This is a manifest-only change: no new backend routes are needed — CRUD flows through the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through proxy with the user's forwarded token, and reads continue to use the existing `/api/featurestores` proxy.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Update `manifests/core-bases/base/sa-rbac/cluster-role.yaml` to add `create, update, patch, delete` verbs for `feast.dev/featurestores` to the dashboard's ClusterRole (it currently grants only `get, list, watch`). Use the feast-operator's `featurestore-editor-role` ClusterRole as the reference for the minimum required permission set.\n39\t- Preserve the viewer tier: non-admin users remain limited to the existing `featurestore-viewer-role` (`get, list, watch` on `featurestores` and `featurestores/status`) — no viewer permission expansion.\n40\t- Add the Feature Store admin UI feature flag default in `OdhDashboardConfig` so clusters without the Feast component enabled see no UI changes (backwards compatibility / progressive rollout).\n41\t- No changes to the Feast CRD schema or operator behavior; no new BFF sidecar or Go module (FIPS posture unchanged).\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- The dashboard ClusterRole grants `create, update, patch, delete` (plus existing read verbs) on `feast.dev/featurestores`, matching or exceeding the `featurestore-editor-role` reference permission set.\n46\t- A user bound only to the viewer role remains unable to create, update, or delete `FeatureStore` CRs via the Kubernetes API (enforcement is at the K8s API level via the forwarded token, not UI hiding).\n47\t- The admin UI is gated behind the `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag and is not visible when the flag is disabled or the Feast component is absent.\n48\t- Manifests render and apply cleanly; no new backend routes, containers, or external network connections are introduced.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- Enables HLR-1 (P0: deploy FeatureStore via dashboard) — write verbs required for create.\n53\t- Enables HLR-4 (P0: delete FeatureStore from dashboard) — delete verb required.\n54\t- Supports HLR-6 (P1: viewers browse but cannot create/delete) — viewer tier stays read-only at the RBAC level.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e24347feee1676f","agent_id":"a232e60a03d76c105","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"e68c7fd2-9692-4be7-a1a7-427b72cc851a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:32:38.933Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bafb6cdf8ea51c36","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8007 decomposition"}
