path: E001→E005→E007→E008 = 4 nodes; or counting edges 3. Summary says 4. M standard: 3-4. Fine.\n7. AC quality: rule-mandated ACs — feature-flag ACs present (E005, E006, E007 verifies). docs review AC in E008 ✓. Rollback/feature-flag for replacements — E004 modifies existing ClusterRole (extension, not replacement); no rollback AC. Hmm, is E004 a \"replacement\"? It extends verbs on an existing role — additive change. The rule 24-26 mandate rollback/feature-flag ACs for replacements; E004 isn't a replacement. And the feature-flag rollout provides the rollback mechanism, covered in E004's AC (\"admin UI gated behind feature flag\"). OK.\n8. Non-testable ACs (external schedule constraints): scan again... E003 AC \"Wireframes ... are delivered and reviewed\" — review is a human process but it's a deliverable AC, testable (review happened or not). E007 \"Dashboard pod resource consumption ... recorded and shows no unexpected growth\" — testable. E001 ACs — deliverable-based. None are lab-turnaround style. OK.\n9. Draft ID references in bodies: grep needed. Let me check \"E00\\d\" in epic bodies.\n10. Component names: validator checked canonical components — E001 \"Feature Store\", E002/E004/E005/E006 \"AI Core Dashboard\", E003 \"UXD\", E007 \"QE\", E008 \"Documentation\". Validator OK.\n11. Signals: need to verify against rubric. Let me read the signal rubric in decompose-agent.md lines ~178-220.\n\nAlso check E002's investigation_signals: cluster_hardware_dependence: 0, human_judgment_required: -1. And E001: cluster_hardware_dependence: -1, human_judgment_required: -1. Need rubric definitions.\n\nAlso E005/E006 ai_signals open_questions: -1. Need rubric: what does -1 mean for open_questions? Let me read the rubric.","signature":"df7ae2539ca14bc6894e529a48dec2de"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41344,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e24347feee1676f","agen