ange downstream scope (Rule 3), E003-E008 produce concrete artifacts. However, there\n92\tis a gate-metadata defect:\n93\t\n94\t- **E005 lists two Investigations in `dependencies` (E001 and E002), and the\n95\t  decomposition summary's own DAG justification characterizes BOTH edges as true gates\n96\t  with action `rewrite` (\"Prototype alignment determines how much of draft PR #7013 can\n97\t  be reused vs rebuilt, changing the wizard implementation approach. True gate, action\n98\t  `rewrite`\"), but E005's `gated_by` records only E001.** The E002 gate on E005 is not\n99\t  expressed in gate metadata, so automated pipeline consumers that detect gates via\n100\t  `gated_by` will miss it — exactly the failure mode the gate fields exist to prevent.\n101\t  E006, by contrast, correctly records `gated_by: E002` for its Investigation dependency.\n102\t  Per the review rules, an Investigation dependency without `gated_by` coverage is a\n103\t  major issue. (Note: `gated_by` is a single-value field, so the revision must either\n104\t  make the E002 → E005 edge a non-gating scheduling dependency with justification, or\n105\t  restructure so the single `gated_by` value covers every Investigation dependency —\n106\t  as written, the summary asserts two true gates but the frontmatter records one.)\n107\t\n108\t`gate_failure_impact` is populated (action + fallback_approach) on both epics that set\n109\t`gated_by`, and both `gated_by` targets appear in the corresponding direct\n110\t`dependencies` lists.\n111\t\n112\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n113\tType-appropriate signal sets are used throughout: `investigation_signals` on E001/E002\n114\t(Investigation), `ai_signals` on E003-E008 (Implementation); no cross-contamination.\n115\tInvestigation signal values match the rubric conditions: E001\n116\t`cluster_hardware_dependence: -1` correctly reflects that the gating questions are\n117\tsource-answerable while peripheral reconciliation/webhook validation needs a live