uling dependency that belongs in `dependencies` only — so\nthis criterion scores 0. Correction: pick one reading (the E005 rationale argues\nboth should be non-gating scheduling dependencies) and align E005/E006 accordingly.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\nType-appropriate signal fields are present and correct throughout: E001/E002 carry\n`investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric); E003-E008 carry `ai_signals` (9-signal\nrubric). All eight ai-signals files exist and their rationale tables match the\nfrontmatter values. Spot checks hold up: E001 `source_accessibility: 1` (public CRD\nschema and operator source) and `human_judgment_required: -1` (PM sign-off on the\nfield subset) are justified; E002 `cluster_hardware_dependence: 0` (code-reading\nassessment) is consistent with its scope; E005/E006 `open_questions: -1` match their\ngated status; E008 `human_process_gates: -1` matches the docs editorial process.\nTwo arguable-but-defensible values noted as minors: E003 `open_questions: 0` (the\nfield-set decision shapes wizard form layout; the \"field set as a design variable\"\nrationale is stated but thin) and E007 `open_questions: 1` (create-wizard test\ncoverage depends on E001's unresolved field-set outcome). Neither contradicts the\nrubric. Arithmetic/thresholds not checked (computed by pipeline).\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy's proposed acceptance\ncriteria. Rule-mandated ACs: the docs-authoring epic (E008) has both technical\nreview by engineering and editorial review ACs; no replacement epics exist (new UI\nsurface — feature-flag ACs are present anyway on E005/E006); no konflux chain\n(build-pipeline AC N/A). The canonical soft-AC trap is handled correctly: the UXD\ntimeline external-schedule constraint sits in E003's Risks/Notes and the summary's\nHealth Warnings, not as an AC. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID\n(epics refer to \"the CRD form-scope investigation\" 