{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0aac910c5c5e621","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E007\n3\ttitle: QE validation of Feature Store admin UI including disconnected environment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: QE\n6\tteam: QE Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E004\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E005\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E006\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: 1\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: 0\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\timplementation_type: null\n24\tinvestigation_signals: null\n25\tai_implementability: High\n26\tai_implementability_score: 6\n27\tjira_key: null\n28\tbranch: null\n29\tgated_by: null\n30\tgate_failure_impact: null\n31\t---\n32\t# QE validation of Feature Store admin UI including disconnected environment\n33\t\n34\t## Description\n35\t\n36\tDelivers the QE validation effort for the Feature Store admin UI: functional testing of the CRUD flows, RBAC enforcement (admin vs. viewer), status-tracking accuracy, and validation of the disconnected/air-gapped deployment scenario. The strategy assigns QE a distinct testing role with its own test suites; this epic runs against the implemented admin UI, the extended dashboard RBAC, and a deployed Feast operator.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Functional test coverage for the create wizard (form submission, CRD schema validation feedback, API rejection surfacing), the management list page, the detail/inspect view, and the delete flow with confirmation.\n41\t- RBAC enforcement testing: admin users can create/delete; viewer (non-admin) users can browse but have no create/delete actions in the UI and cannot write `FeatureStore` CRs via the Kubernetes API even when bypassing the UI (token-level enforcement).\n42\t- Status-tracking accuracy: list status reflects `.status.conditions` within the watch/poll cycle across the deploying → ready progression.\n43\t- Disconnected/air-gapped environment validation: deploy a FeatureStore instance from the dashboard on an air-gapped cluster with no external connectivity, verifying no form options, validation rules, or UI assets require external network access.\n44\t- Feature-flag gating verification: UI hidden when the flag is disabled or the Feast component is absent.\n45\t- Dashboard pod resource monitoring in QE environments (frontend-pages-only change, no new BFF sidecar).\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Test suites covering CRUD flows, viewer/admin RBAC enforcement, and status accuracy pass, with results recorded.\n50\t- A FeatureStore instance is successfully deployed from the dashboard on an air-gapped cluster with no external connectivity — the disconnected-environment acceptance criterion from the strategy is demonstrated end to end.\n51\t- Direct Kubernetes API write attempts by a viewer-role user are rejected (RBAC enforced at the API level, not only UI hiding).\n52\t- Feature-flag gating behaves as specified (no UI changes on clusters without the Feast component enabled).\n53\t- Dashboard pod resource consumption in QE environments is recorded and shows no unexpected growth attributable to the admin UI.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- Validates HLR-1 through HLR-5 (P0: create, list, inspect, delete, status tracking) — functional verification of each flow.\n58\t- Validates HLR-6 (P1: viewer browse-only enforcement, including API-level bypass attempts).\n59\t- Validates HLR-7 (P1: disconnected/air-gapped operation) — the dedicated air-gapped test pass.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6da3b0b539286d2","agent_id":"ac2adcea6f526cc79","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"d9319d00-0631-4ca0-8f94-5f39b6ccb4cd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:49:03.066Z","tool_result_met