{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-896ca1d31428dee9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n3\ttitle: Resolve FeatureStore CRD form scope and operator validation questions\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: Feature Store Engineering\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Resolve FeatureStore CRD form scope and operator validation questions\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the open questions that determine what the Feature Store admin create form exposes and confirm that the existing Feast operator safely handles dashboard-created instances. It produces a single findings-and-recommendations deliverable owned by Feature Store Engineering (with PM input on the field-subset decision) that the dashboard create-wizard implementation builds against. The strategy explicitly flags these as open questions and \"needs validation\" assumptions; their answers change the scope of the guided form wizard, so this is a true gate.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Recommend whether the TP create form should expose the full `FeatureStore` CRD (feast.dev/v1) spec or a curated subset, with the recommended field list and sensible defaults covering: namespace, registry type, online store backend (Redis, PostgreSQL, DynamoDB, SQLite), offline store backend, authorization mode (OIDC vs Kubernetes RBAC), TLS settings, scaling configuration (replicas, HPA), and materialization CronJob scheduling.\n34\t- Document CRD schema constraints the form must enforce (required fields, valid backend combinations, scaling prerequisites), derived from the feast.dev/v1 OpenAPI schema.\n35\t- Identify backend combinations that should be restricted or flagged in the form (e.g., SQLite as development-only, not production-suitable).\n36\t- Confirm the stability of the FeatureStore v1 API for the RHOAI 3.5 cycle (v1alpha1 is deprecated; v1 shipped in 3.5-ea.1 with Feast 0.63.0) and record a version-pin recommendation.\n37\t- Validate that the feast-operator correctly reconciles `FeatureStore` CRs created through the Kubernetes API by the dashboard (not just kubectl/GitOps), and that CRD webhook validation is sufficient for UI-submitted resources — recording a pass/fail result and any gaps.\n38\t- Document CRD field mutability (which fields are immutable after creation) to inform the explicitly deferred follow-on edit capability — informational only, edit is out of TP scope.\n39\t\n40\t## Acceptance Criteria\n41\t\n42\t- A findings document enumerates the recommended form field set with per-field CRD constraints, traceable to the feast.dev/v1 OpenAPI schema.\n43\t- Backend combination restrictions (or guidance flags) are documented with rationale.\n44\t- Operator reconciliation of dashboard-created FeatureStore CRs is exercised on a test cluster and the pass/fail result, including any webhook-validation gaps and their client-side mitigation, is recorded.\n45\t- A CRD stability assessment for the RHOAI 3.5 cycle is recorded with a version-pin recommendation.\n46\t- The curated-subset vs full-field-set decision is recorded with PM sign-off.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- De-risks and shapes HLR-1 (P0: guided create form wizard) — the field-set recommendation defines the wizard's scope.\n51\t- Supports HLR-5 (P0: readiness status from `.status.conditions`) — confirms the status surface the management pages render.\n52\t- Supports HLR-8 (P2: inline validation for CRD schema constraints) — supplies the constraint set the form validates against.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4985b9bc6b60269","agent_id":"ab20d34d2b35722a1","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"fa7a93ae-a0af-4761-9384-d1644003f674","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:53:07.902Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-896ca1d31428dee9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second review of RHAISTRAT-8007"}
