{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a90c4d9ce194b0e1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n3\ttitle: UXD designs for Feature Store admin UI (wizard, list, detail)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: UXD\n6\tteam: UXD Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 0\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# UXD designs for Feature Store admin UI (wizard, list, detail)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDelivers the UX design assets — wireframes and interaction patterns — for the Feature Store admin UI in the RHOAI dashboard: the guided create wizard, the instance management list page, the read-only detail/inspect view, and the delete confirmation dialog. The strategy carries the `needs-uxd` label and lists UXD design as a dependency required before frontend implementation; the frontend epics build against these design assets.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Wireframes and interaction patterns for the guided create form wizard mapping the `FeatureStore` CRD spec (namespace, registry type, online/offline store backends, authorization mode, TLS, scaling, materialization schedule) to a PatternFly 6 form experience.\n38\t- Treat the CRD form-scope investigation's outcome (curated subset vs. full field set) as an explicit design variable rather than an input dependency: the wizard wireframes are drawn for the full CRD spec, organized into grouped form sections that collapse gracefully for a curated subset, so design work proceeds in parallel with that investigation and the final field-set recommendation is applied to the wireframes without redesign.\n39\t- Wireframes and interaction patterns for the management list page (name, namespace, status, creation timestamp, inspect/delete row actions) and the read-only detail view.\n40\t- Interaction pattern for the delete confirmation dialog.\n41\t- State design for deployment progress / readiness presentation (deploying → ready) and for non-admin (viewer) presentation where write controls are hidden.\n42\t- Design guidance for air-gapped suitability (no external assets or network-fetched content in the design).\n43\t- Use the validated engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) as the starting design reference to accelerate the design cycle, per the strategy's risk mitigation.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Wireframes covering the create wizard, list page, detail view, and delete confirmation dialog are delivered and reviewed.\n48\t- Interaction patterns specify the viewer (non-admin) experience with write controls absent, consistent with the admin/viewer authorization model.\n49\t- Designs use bundled PatternFly 6 components only — no external network-fetched assets.\n50\t- Designs are validated against the prototype's screens and the RHOAI dashboard design conventions.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- Enables HLR-1 (P0: guided create form wizard) — wizard design.\n55\t- Enables HLR-2, HLR-3, HLR-4 (P0: list, inspect, delete) — management page designs.\n56\t- Supports HLR-6 (P1: viewer browse without create/delete actions) — viewer state design.\n57\t\n58\t## Risks / Notes\n59\t\n60\t- **UXD timeline is an external schedule constraint.** The strategy carries the `needs-uxd` label but no design sprint is scheduled, and frontend development waits on these design assets. Mitigation (per the strategy's risk table): use the validated engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) as the starting design reference to unblock and accelerate the design cycle while formal designs are created. This risk is tracked at the strategy level in the decomposition summary's Health Warnings and sits on the P0 critical path.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4985b9bc6b60269","agent_id":"ab20d34d2b35722a1","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"374ce86b-7a8d-43b3-bc3a-2796fe84a023","timestamp":"2026-10-22T06:53:12.011Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a90c4d9ce194b0e1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second review of RHAISTRAT-8007"}
