{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ae8d485db9d0f0d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E006\n3\ttitle: 'Feature Store management pages: list, detail/inspect, delete, status tracking'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n12\tgated_by: null\n13\tgate_failure_impact: null\n14\tai_signals:\n15\t  change_specificity: 1\n16\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n17\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n18\t  existing_foundation: 1\n19\t  open_questions: 1\n20\t  external_dependency: 0\n21\t  human_process_gates: 0\n22\t  repo_access: 1\n23\t  architecture_claims: 1\n24\timplementation_type: null\n25\tinvestigation_signals: null\n26\tai_implementability: High\n27\tai_implementability_score: 7\n28\tjira_key: null\n29\tbranch: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Feature Store management pages: list, detail/inspect, delete, status tracking\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tImplements the Feature Store management surface in the RHOAI dashboard: a list page showing all `FeatureStore` instances across namespaces accessible to the user, a read-only detail/inspect view of any instance's full spec and status, an admin-initiated delete flow with confirmation dialog, and real-time deployment-progress tracking from `.status.conditions`. Reads use the existing dashboard K8s watch/list patterns; delete sends a `DELETE` to the Kubernetes API through the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through, with the feast-operator handling resource cleanup via finalizers. Builds against the UXD designs and reuses the validated engineering prototype wherever the alignment assessment confirms it. The prototype alignment assessment is a scheduling input for implementation efficiency, not a scope gate — consistent with its treatment for the create wizard: if it finds the prototype diverges from the formal approach, the pages are built directly on the dashboard's established formal patterns (K8s watch/list, `/api/k8s/*` pass-through) with unchanged scope and acceptance criteria.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Build the management list page per the UXD designs: rows showing name, namespace, deployment status, and creation timestamp, with inspect and delete row actions; scoped to namespaces the user can access.\n40\t- Implement status polling via the dashboard's existing K8s watch/list patterns so readiness state (`.status.conditions`) updates in real time without manual refresh, including the \"Deploying\" → \"Ready\" progression after creation.\n41\t- Build the read-only detail/inspect view: full `FeatureStore` CR spec (online/offline store backends, registry type, authorization mode, scaling, TLS status, materialization schedule) and current status conditions, rendered without truncation; link to the Feast UI Route for browsing feature metadata when available.\n42\t- Implement the delete flow with a confirmation dialog; deletion relies on the feast-operator's finalizer-based cleanup of owned resources (Deployments, Services, ConfigMaps, CronJobs, HPAs, PDBs, RBAC, Routes).\n43\t- Gate write controls (delete action) on platform-admin status; non-admin (viewer) users see list and detail views without write controls.\n44\t- Gate the pages behind the `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag; bundle all assets (air-gapped support); no external network fetches.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- The management page lists all FeatureStore instances in namespaces the admin can access, matching `kubectl get featurestores -A` output for those namespaces, with name, namespace, status, and creation timestamp.\n49\t- After a new instance is created, the list shows it with a deploying status that transitions to ready as `.status.conditions` update, within the dashboard's watch/poll cycle and without manual refresh.\n50\t- The detail view renders all spec fields and status conditions of the `FeatureStore` CR in read-only form without truncation.\n51\t- Delete with confirmation removes the `FeatureStore` CR via the Kubernetes API; the instance disappears from the list and `kubectl get featurestore <name> -n <ns>` returns NotFound, with operator-owned resources cleaned up.\n52\t- A non-admin (viewer) user can browse the list and detail views but sees no delete action.\n53\t- The pages function on a disconnected/air-gapped cluster — no UI assets or data fetches require external network access.\n54\t- The pages are hidden when the feature flag is disabled.\n55\t- End-to-end delete is verified against a cluster with the extended dashboard ClusterRole applied.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-2 (P0): view all FeatureStore instances in a management page.\n60\t- HLR-3 (P0): inspect configuration in a read-only detail view.\n61\t- HLR-4 (P0): delete a FeatureStore instance with confirmation dialog.\n62\t- HLR-5 (P0): deployment progress / readiness visible in real time.\n63\t- HLR-6 (P1, browse portion): viewers can browse list and detail without delete actions.\n64\t- HLR-7 (P1, page portion): functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab37b62e81304a55","agent_id":"a86d0894d521780ff","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"c1913b15-e12b-48c4-8006-12670fabcc27","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:01:59.156Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ae8d485db9d0f0d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Third revision of RHAISTRAT-8007"}
