{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c27515002d60968","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Assess prototype PR #7013 alignment with the formal implementation approach'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Assess prototype PR #7013 alignment with the formal implementation approach\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation determines how much of the validated engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) can be reused for the formal Feature Store admin UI implementation, and whether the prototype's approach matches the strategy's formal path (K8s API pass-through for CRUD, `/api/featurestores` read proxy, `secureAdminRoute` gating, feature-flag rollout). The strategy lists prototype alignment as an assumption needing validation with the Dashboard and Feature Store engineering leads; the answer determines how much prototype code is reused versus rebuilt — a sequencing and efficiency input for the frontend epics. It does not change their scope or acceptance criteria (a divergent prototype means building directly on the formal approach), so both consuming frontend epics record it as a scheduling dependency in `dependencies` only, not as a scope gate.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Review the prototype PR #7013 code against the strategy's formal approach: CRUD via the existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through, reads via the existing `/api/featurestores` proxy, admin/viewer gating via `secureAdminRoute` and the admin status check, and feature-flag gating in `OdhDashboardConfig`.\n34\t- Produce a reuse inventory: which prototype components, hooks, pages, and patterns can be carried into the formal implementation as-is, which need rework, and which diverge from the formal path and must be rebuilt.\n35\t- Identify any architectural divergences (e.g., new backend routes, bypassed RBAC patterns, hardcoded config) and their remediation cost.\n36\t- Record an engineering-lead confirmation (Dashboard + Feature Store) that the prototype may serve as the reference implementation.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A findings document maps each prototype surface (create flow, list, detail, delete, status handling) to a disposition: reuse as-is / rework / rebuild, with rationale.\n41\t- Any divergence between the prototype and the formal approach (API routing, authorization, feature gating) is enumerated with the corrective action required.\n42\t- Engineering-lead sign-off on using the prototype as the implementation reference is recorded.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- De-risks HLR-1 through HLR-5 (P0: create wizard, list page, detail view, delete flow, status tracking) — the alignment finding determines the implementation approach for all admin UI frontend surfaces.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab37b62e81304a55","agent_id":"a86d0894d521780ff","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"df42527d-105f-4187-946c-ef7ba7cce52d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:02:04.391Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c27515002d60968","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Third revision of RHAISTRAT-8007"}
