{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-832b1ef647935dc6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n3\tepic_count: 8\n4\tcritical_path_length: 4\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8007 Feature Store Admin UI\n10\t\n11\tParent strategy: RHAISTRAT-8007 — [TP] Feature Store Admin UI — Self-Service Instance Deployment and Management.\n12\t\n13\tTriage: full decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy is M-effort\n14\t(3-5 sprints), spans multiple architecturally distinct work streams (React frontend pages,\n15\tkustomize/RBAC manifests, UXD design assets, QE validation, admin-guide documentation) and\n16\tmultiple teams (Dashboard/Frontend Engineering, Feature Store Engineering, UXD Team, QE Team,\n17\tDocumentation Team). No Staff Engineer Input was present (template placeholder only), so the\n18\tAI-generated Technical Approach is used as-is with no overrides.\n19\t\n20\t## Epic List\n21\t\n22\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n23\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E001 | Resolve FeatureStore CRD form scope and operator validation questions | Investigation | Feature Store Engineering | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E002 | Assess prototype PR #7013 alignment with the formal implementation approach | Investigation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E003 | UXD designs for Feature Store admin UI (wizard, list, detail) | Implementation | UXD Team | P0 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E004 | Extend odh-dashboard RBAC and feature-flag manifests for Feature Store admin CRUD | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E005 | Feature Store create wizard (guided form) in odh-dashboard | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E006 | Feature Store management pages: list, detail/inspect, delete, status tracking | Implementation | Dashboard/Frontend Engineering | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E007 | QE validation of Feature Store admin UI including disconnected environment | Implementation | QE Team | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-8007-E008 | Document Feature Store admin UI workflow in the RHOAI admin guide | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Documentation Team | P1 |\n32\t\n33\t## Dependency DAG\n34\t\n35\t```mermaid\n36\tgraph TD\n37\t    E001 --> E005\n38\t    E002 --> E005\n39\t    E002 --> E006\n40\t    E003 --> E005\n41\t    E003 --> E006\n42\t    E004 --> E007\n43\t    E005 --> E007\n44\t    E006 --> E007\n45\t    E003 --> E008\n46\t    E004 --> E008\n47\t    E005 --> E008\n48\t    E006 --> E008\n49\t    E007 --> E008\n50\t```\n51\t\n52\t## DAG Justification\n53\t\n54\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n55\t|------|------|-----------|\n56\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The form-scope investigation (curated subset vs full CRD field set, backend combination restrictions, CRD stability, operator/webhook validation) determines what the create wizard builds. True gate, action `rewrite`: a curated-subset outcome re-scopes the wizard's field mapping. |\n57\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 (non-gating scheduling dependency) | Prototype alignment determines how much of draft PR #7013 can be reused vs rebuilt — a sequencing/efficiency input, not a scope gate. The wizard's field set, validation rules, and UX are determined by the CRD form-scope investigation and the UXD designs; if the prototype diverges from the formal approach, the wizard is built directly on the formal approach with unchanged scope and ACs. Kept in `dependencies` only (scheduling); `gated_by` is single-value and records the scope-determining gate (the CRD form-scope investigation). |\n58\t| E002 → E006 | Rule 3 (non-gating scheduling dependency) | Same alignment finding as for the create wizard: reuse-vs-rebuild is a sequencing/efficiency input, not a scope gate. The pages' scope and ACs are unchanged by a divergent prototype — they would be built directly on the dashboard's established K8s list/detail/watch patterns instead of carrying prototype code. Kept in `dependencies` only (scheduling), aligned with the E002 → E005 edge; E006 has no scope-determining gate, since the detail view renders the full CR spec regardless of the form-scope outcome. |\n59\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 12 (producer → consumer) | The wizard is built against the UXD wireframes and interaction patterns; design assets are a build-against artifact. |\n60\t| E003 → E006 | Rule 12 | The management pages (list, detail, delete confirmation) are built against the same UXD designs. |\n61\t| E004 → E007 | Rule 12 | QE validates admin-vs-viewer RBAC enforcement, which requires the extended ClusterRole and feature flag to be in place. |\n62\t| E005 → E007 | Rule 12 | QE functionally validates the built create flow. |\n63\t| E006 → E007 | Rule 12 | QE functionally validates the built list/detail/delete/status flows. |\n64\t| E003/E004/E005/E006/E007 → E008 | Rule 11 (docs last) | The docs-authoring epic is blocked by every main-plan Implementation epic; docs describe what was built. |\n65\t| (no edge) E004 ↔ E005/E006 | Rule 10 analog (config vs code) | The RBAC/feature-flag manifest change is configuration the frontend does not build against; frontend pages are developed against the existing generic `/api/k8s/*` pass-through. Coupling is enforced by an acceptance criterion on the frontend epics (\"end-to-end CRUD verified against a cluster with the extended ClusterRole applied\"), not a DAG edge — an edge would serialize parallel work. |\n66\t| (no edge) E001 → E006 | — | The management pages render the full CR spec and `.status.conditions` — no curation decision needed; the detail view is unaffected by the form-scope outcome. |\n67\t| (no edge) E001 → E003 | — | The wizard design treats the form-scope field set as an explicit design variable (see E003 scope): wireframes are drawn for the full CRD spec as grouped form sections that collapse gracefully for a curated subset, so UXD proceeds in parallel with the investigation and the field-set recommendation is applied to the wireframes without redesign. |\n68\t| (no edge) E005 ↔ E006 | Rule 15 | Same repo, different UI surfaces (create wizard vs management pages); parallel with coordination risk only. |\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n71\t\n72\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n73\t|-----|----------|---------|\n74\t| HLR-1: Deploy new FeatureStore via guided form wizard | P0 | E005 |\n75\t| HLR-2: View all FeatureStore instances in management page | P0 | E006 |\n76\t| HLR-3: Inspect configuration in read-only detail view | P0 | E006 |\n77\t| HLR-4: Delete FeatureStore with confirmation dialog | P0 | E006 |\n78\t| HLR-5: Deployment progress / readiness visible in real time | P0 | E006 |\n79\t| HLR-6: Viewers can browse but not create/delete | P1 | E005 (create action hidden), E006 (browse + delete action hidden) |\n80\t| HLR-7: Functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments | P1 | E005 (bundled form assets), E006 (no external fetches), E007 (air-gapped validation) |\n81\t| HLR-8: Inline guidance for CRD schema constraints | P2 | E005 (bundled — same form surface as HLR-1, not independently shippable) |\n82\t\n83\tAll 8 HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. HLR-8 (P2) is bundled into the P0 wizard epic\n84\tbecause inline validation is incidental to the same form implementation surface — splitting it\n85\twould produce two epics building the same form. HLR-6 and HLR-7 are cross-cutting P1s mapped as\n86\tacceptance criteria on each affected surface epic plus QE validation, not separate epics.\n87\t\n88\t## Health Warnings\n89\t\n90\t- **UXD timeline is an external schedule constraint, not an epic.** The `needs-uxd` label is\n91\t  present and no design sprint is scheduled; the strategy's own mitigation (use prototype\n92\t  PR #7013 as the starting design reference) is recorded as a risk note on the design epic.\n93\t  Watch this on the P0 critical path.\n94\t- **Edit-capability contradiction.** The Out-of-Scope section defers in-place editing of\n95\t  deployed FeatureStore CRs to a follow-on, but an open question still asks whether edit should\n96\t  be in TP. Resolved per Out-of-Scope (create + inspect + delete only); CRD field mutability is\n97\t  documented informationally by the CRD-scope investigation to inform the follow-on.\n98\t- **feast-operator is passive but validated by a different team.** Per the strategy, no operator\n99\t  code changes are expected; the required validation (reconciliation of dashboard-created CRs,\n100\t  webhook validation sufficiency) is folded into the CRD-scope Investigation (E001) rather than a\n101\t  separate validation Implementation epic, because the validation outcome is itself an open\n102\t  question and its failure mode is already mitigated by the strategy (derive form validation from\n103\t  the CRD OpenAPI schema and surface K8s API rejection in the UI). If the investigation finds\n104\t  operator-side gaps, remediation work should be raised as a follow-up.\n105\t- **No performance-target epic.** The open question on performance targets is answered by the\n106\t  strategy's NFR/prerequisites sections (low-frequency admin CRUD, Performance Team Support \"Not\n107\t  applicable\" for TP). If targets are later specified, they become acceptance criteria on the\n108\t  frontend epics, not new epics.\n109\t- **Architecture Review is pending human review** at the strategy level — a process gate outside\n110\t  this decomposition's control.\n111\t- **Non-obvious canonical component mappings** (strategy name → RHAI Jira component):\n112\t  odh-dashboard → `AI Core Dashboard`; feast-operator → `Feature Store`; design assets → `UXD`;\n113\t  test suites → `QE`; admin guides → `Documentation`.\n114\t\n115\t## Tiered Delivery\n116\t\n117\tNot applicable. No external dependency has uncertain timing: the FeatureStore CRD (feast.dev/v1)\n118\tand feast-operator reconciliation already ship in RHOAI 3.5-ea.1, the `/api/k8s/*` and\n119\t`/api/featurestores` dashboard routes exist, and PatternFly 6 (v6.4.x) is already in\n120\todh-dashboard. The only external-input item (UXD design) is modeled as a blocking epic (E003)\n121\twith the prototype-as-reference mitigation, not a tiered split.\n122\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab37b62e81304a55","agent_id":"a86d0894d521780ff","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"edc0147e-ecf2-4549-ab12-3d582519dc1f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:02:12.468Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-832b1ef647935dc6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Third revision of RHAISTRAT-8007"}
