{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a34e157263ce6993","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8007-E005\n3\ttitle: Feature Store create wizard (guided form) in odh-dashboard\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8007\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard/Frontend Engineering\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8007-E003\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8007-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: 'Covers both gating investigations. If the CRD form-scope investigation\n17\t    lands on a different field set or new backend restrictions, re-scope the wizard\n18\t    fields and validation to its outcome; if it finds the CRD unstable for 3.5, pin\n19\t    form validation to the v1 OpenAPI schema revision shipped in 3.5-ea.1 and surface\n20\t    API rejection errors in the UI. If the prototype alignment assessment finds draft\n21\t    PR #7013 diverges from the formal approach, build the wizard directly on the formal\n22\t    approach (K8s API pass-through, PatternFly 6 form patterns, secureAdminRoute gating)\n23\t    instead of reusing prototype components - an approach change (reuse vs rebuild)\n24\t    with scope and acceptance criteria unchanged.'\n25\tai_signals:\n26\t  change_specificity: 1\n27\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n28\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n29\t  existing_foundation: 1\n30\t  open_questions: -1\n31\t  external_dependency: 0\n32\t  human_process_gates: 0\n33\t  repo_access: 1\n34\t  architecture_claims: 1\n35\timplementation_type: null\n36\tinvestigation_signals: null\n37\tai_implementability: High\n38\tai_implementability_score: 5\n39\tjira_key: null\n40\tbranch: null\n41\t---\n42\t# Feature Store create wizard (guided form) in odh-dashboard\n43\t\n44\t## Description\n45\t\n46\tImplements the guided create-form wizard that lets a platform administrator deploy a new Feature Store instance from the RHOAI dashboard without YAML editing or CLI access. The wizard is a PatternFly 6 React form mapping to the `FeatureStore` CRD spec (feast.dev/v1), submitting a validated custom resource to the Kubernetes API through the dashboard's existing `/api/k8s/*` pass-through proxy using the user's forwarded token. Builds against the UXD designs and the CRD field-scope recommendations, and reuses the validated engineering prototype (odh-dashboard draft PR #7013) wherever the alignment assessment confirms fit. This epic is gated by both upstream investigations: the CRD form-scope investigation is the recorded gate (`gated_by`), and its recorded gate-failure fallback covers both gate outcomes — a different field set or backend restrictions re-scope the wizard's fields and validation, and a divergent prototype means the wizard is built directly on the formal approach with unchanged scope and acceptance criteria (an approach change: reuse vs rebuild).\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Build the create wizard per the UXD designs: fields for namespace selection, registry type, online store backend, offline store backend, authorization mode, and scaling parameters, mapped to the `FeatureStore` CRD spec.\n51\t- Implement the field set and defaults recommended by the CRD form-scope investigation (curated subset or full spec, per its outcome), including any backend-combination restrictions or guidance it identifies.\n52\t- Validate inputs against CRD schema constraints before submission with inline guidance (required fields, valid backend combinations, scaling prerequisites), and surface Kubernetes API / webhook rejection errors in the UI after submission.\n53\t- Gate the create action on platform-admin status (`secureAdminRoute` middleware plus the frontend admin check); non-admin (viewer) users do not see the create action.\n54\t- Bundle all form options, definitions, and validation rules in the dashboard's static assets — no external network fetches (air-gapped support).\n55\t- Gate the wizard behind the `OdhDashboardConfig` feature flag.\n56\t- Reuse prototype components where the alignment assessment confirms architectural fit.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A platform admin can complete the wizard and submit a valid `FeatureStore` CR to the Kubernetes API from the dashboard — no YAML editing or CLI access required; the form renders all required CRD fields per the investigation's field-set recommendation without error.\n61\t- Invalid input is blocked before submission with inline guidance derived from the CRD schema; if the Kubernetes API rejects a submitted CR, the validation error is surfaced in the UI.\n62\t- The wizard functions on a disconnected/air-gapped cluster — no form options, validation rules, or UI assets require external network access.\n63\t- A non-admin (viewer) user does not see the create action.\n64\t- The wizard is hidden when the feature flag is disabled.\n65\t- End-to-end create is verified against a cluster with the extended dashboard ClusterRole applied (write verbs on `feast.dev/featurestores`).\n66\t- Implementation follows the formal approach (K8s API pass-through, no new backend routes, no new BFF sidecar).\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-1 (P0): deploy a new FeatureStore instance via guided form wizard.\n71\t- HLR-6 (P1, viewer portion): create action hidden for non-admin users.\n72\t- HLR-7 (P1, form portion): functions in disconnected/air-gapped environments.\n73\t- HLR-8 (P2): inline guidance for CRD schema constraints — bundled here because it is the same form surface as HLR-1.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8cac59df77ea9c9","agent_id":"a6f9602b0bf687079","session_id":"5b25fd68-a792-4553-b4a0-957d31cb4ef6","uuid":"14caa9e3-2428-40b0-8377-9230d42a6f22","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:05:11.892Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a34e157263ce6993","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Third review of RHAISTRAT-8007"}
